    Small buffers' copies in the card's memory (VICTORY_CARD_BUFFERS_MIN_KB), changed_runs by masks, scalar buffer loads four dwords a call (VICTORY_SHADER_OPT bit 64), a measuring step for the copy-back (VICTORY_BACK_READS)
    
    - VICTORY_CARD_BUFFERS_MIN_KB=64 (off by default): every title buffer's copy in the card's memory;
      measured at like draws: the title's lists 68.0 -> 49.8 ms of card time a frame, frame 114.9 ->
      109.7 ms. VICTORY_CARD_HASH_LEN=1 (off): the card's hashes cover the title buffer's own bytes.
      A log line says where copies went, by size.
    - changed_runs 64 bytes at a time by a mask of differing bytes (default; =0 the walk, =alt in turn).
    - Shaders: the dwords of one console load by one call for every four (bit 64, not in the default):
      with the bit off the whole pack's output is byte-identical to the build before.
    - VICTORY_BACK_READS=1|2|alt (diagnostics): who touches what the copy-back stored.
    - Frame shots are named with the time they began.
    - README: runs 274 and 275.
    
    Game runs: the changes ran in runs 274 and 275 (the hash switch and the read-back switch of pull
    request #999 not yet). In this tree the diagnostics build finishes; its unit tests were not run
    after the merge (they passed in the tree the changes came from).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

